# Nissan Qashqai J12 five-door crossover, 2021-.
#
# The third-generation Qashqai. The 2021 launch car is modelled; the 2024
# facelift's patterned grille and separated light strips are not.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Qashqai
#
# Dimensions 4.425 x 1.835 x 1.625 m, wheelbase 2.665 m, from the English
# Wikipedia J12 dimension box. Mirrors take the modelled width to 2.080 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the J12 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names: white, grey, blue and black. Weights white 3, grey 3, blue 2,
# black 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 200 km/h for the 1.3 DIG-T mild hybrid, the volume model. Comfort
# 100/330, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 100, a step above the J11's 95/320. Classes
# 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: July 2021 intro, retires staggered 2036-2039 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail, so every colourway is current in 2026.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-qashqai-j12.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-qashqai-j12.dae (56 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-qashqai-j12/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the body is more planar at the sides and bumpers than the
# photographs, and the pack mixes the 2021 and 2024 noses, of which only the
# launch car is modelled. At 128 px the upright tail, the angular split lamps and
# the chrome V grille read as the J12.

obj=citycar
name=NissanQashqaiJ12(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2021
intro_month=7
retire_year=2039
retire_month=6
speed=200
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=100
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=330

